<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallahi ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1846–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Khalifa Abdallahi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallahi ibn Muhammad, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a>, was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdist-state">Mahdist State</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> from 1885 to 1898. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baggara-arabs">Baggara</a> Arab from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a>, he was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>'s chief lieutenant and succeeded him on his death, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omdurman">Omdurman</a>. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and crushed internal revolts, but his army was destroyed by Kitchener at Omdurman in 1898, and he was killed at Umm Diwaykarat in 1899.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdallahi-ibn-muhammad.jpg" alt="Abdallahi ibn Muhammad" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siegfried Weiß · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdallahi_ibn_Muhammad,_1846-1899.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
